            "text_8kEdFg": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<h3>The Early Years — 1950s</h3><p>Women’s wrestling developed a strong following in the United States during the 1950s. Surviving black-and-white footage captures wrestlers who had clearly invested considerable time and skill in their craft.</p><p>The ringwear reflected the conventions of the period, with many costumes featuring skirted fronts and relatively modest silhouettes. These early designs provide a fascinating starting point for the evolution of women’s wrestling attire.</p>",
